Appointment on another post during which the condition necessary for eligibility for the benefit of the next below rule
would operate;
(iv)
Foreign service during which but for such service the absorbed employee would have continued to officiate in such post;
(v)
Suspension followed by reinstatement in the same post where period of suspension is treated as duty or leave;
(vi)
Deputation on training during which period the absorbed employee was considered as on duty and would have officiated
in the post but for such training;
(vii)
Such joining time during which the absorbed employee would have continued to hold the same post;
(8)
"Post of absorption" means the cadre of the post in the authority in which an absorbed employee is absorbed or is
deemed to have been absorbed, irrespective of whether the post is permanent or temporary;
(II)
Words and expressions used in these rules, but not defined herein, shall have the meanings, respectively assigned to
them in the Act.
